{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/typed/load.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T13:34:01.715551Z","id":"7036d7cd330636687725cdc34e3222d4b55161ca5835b486de881ec6e04bbedb","body":{"detail":"provium/src/typed/load.rs resolves paths through module scopes and use declarations, and provium/src/typed/emit.rs infers local types from annotations, signatures and operations. A resolution or method-dispatch mistake that still elaborates in Lean would translate a different program; differential scenarios (provium/src/typed/verify.rs, `differential`) only sample behaviour.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"07c4be93dfc7afbe0ecc71ce16b575acf9e51db0ec0cfbc3dccac164776683a2"},"suggested_fix":"Cross-check resolved callee paths and inferred local types against rustc output for the captured build (for example -Zunpretty=thir-tree or a rustc_public driver), or prove the translation against a formal Rust semantics (CORRECTNESS_PLAN P10).","summary":"The typed backend's name resolution and local type inference are trusted, not checked against rustc","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/typed/load.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-05T04:40:14.755907Z","id":"12f4fd146a4866444e483a63015bdb5e7cd995ab614870ce924871c6e349a36e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fc9f224","summary":"Name resolution and local type inference are now checked against rustc: provium/src/typed/mircheck.rs compares every translated function's crate calls and source-named local types with --emit=mir output of the captured build (jarl/proofs/engine: 95 functions, 194 calls, 379 local types agree; tests/typed.rs rustc_cross_check_catches_misresolved_calls_and_mistyped_locals shows tampered facts are rejected). The remaining unchecked front-end decisions are recorded as a narrower concern on mircheck.rs.","supersedes":"7036d7cd330636687725cdc34e3222d4b55161ca5835b486de881ec6e04bbedb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/typed/mircheck.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-05T04:40:14.794349Z","id":"dd7f4fbb8ce3b0fc472e8f88c93d517068a15f864040aa3c691b564adbb49133","body":{"detail":"provium/src/typed/mircheck.rs compares, per translated function, the crate functions called and the types of source-named locals with rustc's MIR. It does not check the types of intermediate expressions, which Rust operation each expression became (e.g. wrapping vs checked arithmetic, which core method a call dispatches to), calls into core/std, or the 18 Jarl locals whose translated type has no rustc counterpart (iterators, closures, deferred items). A translation that resolves and types every named local correctly but emits the wrong operation is still only caught by the proofs, the differential scenario and the negative controls.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"bc4edb768a8702eec95be46b706e3af297884ff7b9674fff2340a82e9b4e0e6d"},"suggested_fix":"Compare MIR statement-level operations (binary ops with overflow checks, casts, calls to core methods) against the translation's emitted operations, e.g. by recording an operation trace per function in the generator and matching it to MIR's checked/unchecked BinaryOp and Call terminators.","summary":"The rustc cross-check covers calls and named-local types, not expression-level translation","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/typed/diffcov.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-05T04:51:42.538004Z","id":"636587c2fa3ed3d19b0ab3014f6249680a223a404040b6bea0bc0b2017d4406f","body":{"detail":"provium/src/typed/diffcov.rs attributes native llvm-cov regions to translated functions, so a run that executes every region can still leave some Rust.lean definitions (a particular overflow path of Rust.add, a slice helper's out-of-range branch) unexercised in Lean. Rust.lean's own lemmas pin many definitions (e.g. val_saturating_sub), but the differential cannot vouch for the rest. Jarl's run also leaves 111 of 1850 regions unexecuted (Node::send, State::truncate, BatchRollback::drop, Node::compact error paths among them).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"c9529ce73b8ca4116bfc74fa279fc212d44d62f6af08859b72c49c0010897d8b"},"suggested_fix":"Instrument the Lean evaluation (count calls per Rust.lean definition, e.g. with dbgTrace in an instrumented copy of the runtime used only for the differential) and require each definition the translation uses to run; add scenarios aimed at the least-covered functions the report lists.","summary":"Differential coverage is measured per Rust function and region, not per Rust.lean operation","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/src/typed/diffcov.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-05T05:03:31.346349Z","id":"bbc223a50adec26ea91a28ee16dd71ba60aacb38443ace5b3bbee028c4f4051d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"636587c2fa3ed3d19b0ab3014f6249680a223a404040b6bea0bc0b2017d4406f","summary":"Update at git:fe2d3cc: Jarl's widened scenario leaves 58 of 1850 regions unexecuted (was 111). Most remaining regions are defensive (unreachable!, u64 exhaustion guards, BatchRollback's unfinished branch, which needs a mid-batch push failure the count check prevents); the reachable remainder is stale snapshot installs (node.rs:541-548), Full rejections (node.rs:959), extra replies (node.rs:233) and request_from (node.rs:1032). The Rust.lean operation-level gap this thread records is unchanged.","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
